        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(auto-reply): keep export tree truncation UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe exported session HTML tree preview must truncate long node text without breaking emoji or other supplementary-plane characters, and it must not scan or allocate the entire message just to keep the first 100 preview characters. The first code-point-safe implementation used `Array.from(s)` over the full message text, which could make large session exports stall or allocate heavily.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe follow-up replaces full-string materialization with a bounded `for...of` scan that stops at the preview budget and slices by the resulting UTF-16 offset. This preserves code-point-safe truncation and the existing `...` suffix while avoiding full traversal/allocation of large message content.\n\n## User Impact\n\n`/export-session` HTML tree previews keep emoji boundaries intact and remain responsive when a session contains very large message text.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact reviewed head after bot follow-up: `2c85cc6104a`\n- `git diff --check`: pass\n- `corepack pnpm exec oxlint src/auto-reply/reply/export-html/template.js src/auto-reply/reply/export-html/template.security.test.ts`: pass\n- `corepack pnpm exec oxfmt --check src/auto-reply/reply/export-html/template.js src/auto-reply/reply/export-html/template.security.test.ts`: no formatting target because these export-html files are ignored by oxfmt in this checkout, not a formatting failure\n- Real-browser proof: generated a session export HTML with a tree message shaped as `99 x chars + U+1F600 + 500000 y chars`, opened the generated file in headless system Chrome through Playwright, and captured `.tree-content` from the rendered page:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"text\": \"user: xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx??...\",\n  \"codePoints\": 109,\n  \"containsEmoji\": true,\n  \"emojiHex\": \"1f600\",\n  \"containsEllipsisSuffix\": true,\n  \"containsLongTail\": false,\n  \"loneSurrogate\": false\n}\n```\n\n- Local proof artifact generated but not committed: `.tmp-proof-106400/large-tree-export.html` and `.tmp-proof-106400/large-tree-export.png`.\n- Regression coverage now includes the original emoji-boundary tree preview plus a large-message tree preview that asserts the long tail does not leak into the rendered preview.\n\nKnown proof gap: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/export-html/template.security.test.ts -- --testNamePattern \"tree node truncation\"` did not return output before the local 180s timeout in this Windows worktree, so the current update does not claim a fresh local Vitest pass. CI should provide the full test signal for the pushed head.\n",
        "branch": "codex/export-html-truncate-utf16",
